{"title":"1992 AJHSME Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/a/48a018e84e421aaed03f4192d4e70246b227fec7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(ellipse((0,-5),10,3)); fill((-10,-5)--(10,-5)--(10,5)--(-10,5)--cycle,white); draw(ellipse((0,0),10,3)); draw((10,0)--(10,-5)); draw((-10,0)--(-10,-5));  draw((0,0)--(7,-3*sqrt(51)/10)); label(&quot;10&quot;,(7/2,-3*sqrt(51)/20),NE); label(&quot;5&quot;,(-10,-3),E); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"165\" />\n</p><p>Which cylinder has twice the volume of the cylinder shown above?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/4/1349b963179bfa1b7e83dca7b965388f5d7832b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(4);  draw(ellipse((0,-5),20,6)); fill((-20,-5)--(20,-5)--(20,5)--(-20,5)--cycle,white); draw(ellipse((0,0),20,6)); draw((20,0)--(20,-5)); draw((-20,0)--(-20,-5)); draw((0,0)--(14,-3*sqrt(51)/5)); label(&quot;20&quot;,(7,-3*sqrt(51)/10),NE); label(&quot;5&quot;,(-20,-4),E); label(&quot;(A)&quot;,(0,6),N);  draw(ellipse((31,-7),10,3)); fill((21,-7)--(41,-7)--(41,7)--(21,7)--cycle,white); draw(ellipse((31,3),10,3)); draw((41,3)--(41,-7)); draw((21,3)--(21,-7)); draw((31,3)--(38,3-3*sqrt(51)/10)); label(&quot;10&quot;,(34.5,3-3*sqrt(51)/20),NE); label(&quot;10&quot;,(21,-4),E); label(&quot;(B)&quot;,(31,6),N);  draw(ellipse((47,-15.5),5,3/2)); fill((42,-15.5)--(42,-15.5)--(42,15.5)--(42,15.5)--cycle,white); draw(ellipse((47,4.5),5,3/2)); draw((42,4.5)--(42,-15.5)); draw((52,4.5)--(52,-15.5)); draw((47,4.5)--(50.5,4.5-3*sqrt(51)/20)); label(&quot;5&quot;,(48.75,4.5-3*sqrt(51)/40),NE); label(&quot;10&quot;,(42,-6),E); label(&quot;(C)&quot;,(47,6),N);  draw(ellipse((73,-10),20,6)); fill((53,-10)--(93,-10)--(93,5)--(53,5)--cycle,white); draw(ellipse((73,0),20,6)); draw((53,0)--(53,-10)); draw((93,0)--(93,-10)); draw((73,0)--(87,-3*sqrt(51)/5)); label(&quot;20&quot;,(80,-3*sqrt(51)/10),NE); label(&quot;10&quot;,(53,-6),E); label(&quot;(D)&quot;,(73,6),N); [/asy]\" width=\"755\" height=\"218\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f906714028f53f5f5b6f648e562c499b52658846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(E)}\\ \\text{None of the above}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Recall that a cylinder with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> has volume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/a/7eaca10208a9f29e371948f48ab20dc101cb5b95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V = \\pi r^2 h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>The original cylinder thus has volume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb373ca9ba32e4aa3a51b11cfda431fd8530d498.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />, while the cylinders in choices (A), (B), (C), and (D) have volumes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cbc519754cc32c40d58b243d1f119da59688810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2000\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/8/68804a57deb1c3d252ab11fe5bc4dc82994237dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/e/43e145c9e4795b5a2efdf6bf211b1cf45cf39dbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$250\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/2270942a50ef58dfbfcb7266ad4202ac9a1ad2ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4000\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> respectively.  So only the cylinder in choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" /> has twice the volume of the original cylinder.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The volume of a cylinder is directly proportional to both its height and the square of its radius.\n</p><p>The cylinder in choice (A) has the same height as and twice the radius of the original, so its volume is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cb0e6e64d73bacef9c8869039bc21581f1884e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> times that of the original.\n</p><p>The cylinder in choice (B) has twice the height of and the same radius as the original, so its volume is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times that of the original.\n</p><p>The cylinder in choice (C) has twice the height of and half the radius of the original, so its volume is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48c7e5a6fb711de46997374cff2122cfc5bb5771.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"108\" height=\"48\" /> of that of the original.\n</p><p>The cylinder in choice (D) has twice the height of and twice the radius of the original, so its volume is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7fd434efe9b4640f4f32db37b7917ce101d4ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 2^2 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"17\" /> times that of the original.\n</p><p>Therefore, only the cylinder in choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" /> has twice the volume of the original cylinder.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME\" title=\"1992 AJHSME\">1992 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1992\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Problems/Probl